{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>חבב.</b> He is Yitro, as it says ״מִבְּנֵי חֹבָב חֹתֵן מֹשֶׁה״ (Judges 4). And what does Scripture mean by ״וְתָבֹאנָה אֶל רְעוּאֵל אֲבִיהֶן״? It teaches that little children call their grandfather 'Father.' And he had many names: 'Yitro' — because he added (יִתֵּר) one passage in the Torah; 'חוֹבָב' — because he loved (חִבֵּב) the Torah, etc. (Sifrei)." "<b>נוסעים אנחנו אל המקום.</b> Immediately — within three days we are entering the Land, for in this first journey they set out intending to enter the Land of Israel, except that they sinned with the complainers. And why does Moses include himself with them? Because the decree had not yet been decreed upon him, and he thought he was entering (see there)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:13.819661269Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}